Bootstrap: docker
From: ubuntu:24.04

# =============================================================================
# bx_atac_qc / DEF version 1.0
#
# [PURPOSE AND TARGET SCRIPTS]
#   Targets: ATAC_QC.1.0.R and ATAC_QC_plot.1.0.R (the supplied scripts).
#   Both scripts share one R/Bioconductor runtime, so one image serves both.
#   ATAC_QC.1.0.R: fragment size distribution, ATACseqQC::bamQC, Tn5 shift
#   (shiftGAlignmentsList), and nucleosome-position splitting
#   (splitGAlignmentsByCut) of pre-shift, organellar-filtered BAM files.
#   ATAC_QC_plot.1.0.R: TSS enrichment heatmaps and profiles from the split
#   BAM files and split objects written by ATAC_QC.1.0.R.
#   The analysis scripts are supplied through CLOSHA's external bind paths,
#   rather than embedded in the image. This DEF provides their runtime.
#
# [INPUT AND OUTPUT STRUCTURE]
#   ATAC_QC.1.0.R
#     Input: input_dir with pre-shift BAM files (preferably
#     *_organellar_removed.bam), sample_data CSV (SampleID, Condition,
#     Replicate), txs_bed (BED, 3+ columns), genome_fasta, optional seqlev.
#     Missing BAI files are created beside the input BAM files, and a missing
#     FASTA index (.fai) is created beside genome_fasta, so those locations
#     must be writable unless the indexes already exist.
#     Output: 01_fragment_size, 02_bam_qc, 03_shifted_bam, 04_split_bam,
#     05_metadata (resolved sample sheet, atac_qc_manifest.tsv), 06_rds,
#     and logs/.
#   ATAC_QC_plot.1.0.R
#     Input: an ATAC_QC output directory (05_metadata/atac_qc_manifest.tsv,
#     or legacy 04_metadata) and tss_bed; optional upstream, downstream,
#     ntile, tss_filter, and harmonize_mode. BAM and RDS paths are read from
#     the manifest, so the runtime bind must expose the same paths.
#     Output: 01_tss_signal (PDF/TSV), 02_signal_matrices (RDS),
#     03_summary (TSV), and logs/.
#   Both scripts first remove existing output_dir contents except logs/.
#   output_dir must not be an input directory or any parent of an input.
#
# [REQUIRED RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES]
#   R 4.6.1 (Rscript).
#   Bioconductor 3.23, with direct dependencies loaded by the scripts:
#     ATACseqQC (1.36.x), ChIPpeakAnno (3.46.x), Rsamtools, GenomicAlignments,
#     GenomicRanges, GenomeInfoDb, IRanges.
#   All pkg::function calls used by the scripts were checked statically
#   against the NAMESPACE files of the Bioconductor 3.23 source packages.
#   Base R only otherwise (utils, stats, graphics, grDevices pdf device).
#   The recursive dependency set is about 160 CRAN/Bioconductor packages,
#   built from source. System libraries were selected from that set:
#   libcurl, OpenSSL, libxml2, libpng, ICU, GSL, libuv, zlib, bzip2, xz,
#   libdeflate, zstd, and cmake (used by Rhdf5lib through biocmake).
#   The supplied scripts have no command-line tool or Python dependencies.
#   Runtime analysis needs no network access; no annotation downloads occur.
#
# [BASE IMAGE AND INSTALLATION RULES FOR THIS DEF]
#   Base image: the official ubuntu:24.04 image from Docker Hub.
#   OS packages: Ubuntu APT repositories.
#   R: the CRAN Ubuntu APT repository (noble-cran40), pinned to
#   r-base-core/r-base-dev 4.6.1-6.2404.0. The repository key is
#   Michael Rutter's CRAN key, fingerprint
#   E298A3A825C0D65DFD57CBB651716619E084DAB9 (expires 2027-09-30). The key
#   file is checked against the SHA256 value below before it is trusted.
#   R packages: BiocManager from CRAN, then Bioconductor 3.23 packages and
#   their CRAN dependencies from bioconductor.org and cloud.r-project.org.
#   No Conda / Miniconda / Miniforge / Mamba / Micromamba installation is used.
#   No installation step uses repo.anaconda.com or the Anaconda defaults channel.
#   Building requires internet access to Ubuntu, CRAN, and Bioconductor.
#
# [HPC BUILD REQUIREMENTS]
#   Use a designated build environment and an unprivileged build account.
#   Do not run the build as the host root user or through sudo.
#   Do not bind production data or service directories into the build container.
#   Host-side %pre and %setup sections are not used.
#   Package installation, compilation, and cleanup run inside %post.
#   Build workspace: the fixed container-private path /__closha_build/work.
#   /__closha_build and the workspace are created with plain mkdir (no -p),
#   so the build stops if either already exists, including as a symlink or
#   a bind mount point. The APT package cache (Dir::Cache), APT index lists
#   (Dir::State::lists), the CRAN key download, R temporary files (TMPDIR),
#   R user cache/data/config directories, the biocmake cache, and HOME for
#   the install steps are all placed below it.
#   Cleanup removes only that exact workspace, after separate checks of the
#   path constant, symlinks, canonical path, and root-filesystem device, and
#   then removes the empty /__closha_build with rmdir. Any failed check stops
#   the build without deleting anything.
#   No wildcard cleanup of default paths is used; apt-get clean and
#   /var/lib/apt/lists/* cleanup are unnecessary and not used.
#   The base image may ship APT cleanup hooks (for example docker-clean);
#   they were not inspected and must be reviewed with the base image.
#   These checks reduce accidents but do not prove host isolation. The build
#   service must keep host binds off /__closha_build, its parents, and children.
#   No broad cleanup of /tmp, /var/tmp, /root, or user home directories is used.
#   %test performs checks without creating or deleting data files.
#   The Apptainer output SIF, image cache, and build temporary files are host
#   artifacts; place them in an approved build workspace, separate from services.
#   This DEF does not clean the host's Apptainer cache or build workspace.
#   The build service must enforce account, workspace, and mount restrictions;
#   comments in this DEF cannot enforce the host's bind configuration.
#   Compiling about 160 R packages from source takes substantial CPU time;
#   the build service should apply its CPU, memory, and time limits.
#
# [RUNTIME ENVIRONMENT ISOLATION]
#   Apptainer binds the user's home directory by default. %environment points
#   R_LIBS_USER at the image site library and sets R_PROFILE_USER and
#   R_ENVIRON_USER to /dev/null, and unsets R_LIBS, so that a host
#   ~/R library, ~/.Rprofile, or ~/.Renviron is not loaded into this runtime.
#
# [CHANGES FROM THE PREVIOUS SIF]
#   No previous SIF or DEF for these scripts was supplied.
#   This is a new image; nothing existing is modified or overwritten.
#
# [VALIDATION STATUS AND REPRODUCIBILITY]
#   Checked: supplied-script dependencies (library/requireNamespace/::),
#   exports of every pkg::function call in the Bioconductor 3.23 NAMESPACE
#   files, the recursive R dependency set and its Ubuntu 24.04 system
#   requirements, the CRAN key fingerprint and SHA256, and availability of
#   the pinned r-base-core/r-base-dev versions in noble-cran40.
#   Checked: DEF %post and %test shell syntax (sh -n) only.
#   Not performed: an actual Apptainer SIF build, %test run, or analysis
#   validation using the user's BAM files.
#   Production /etc/apptainer/apptainer.conf (supplied by the user):
#   mount home/tmp/proc/sys/dev = yes, bind path = /etc/localtime and
#   /etc/hosts, user bind control = yes, allow setuid = yes.
#   Per Apptainer source (main branch, internal/pkg/build and
#   apptainerconf.ApplyBuildConfig), %post runs with a default config that
#   drops bind path, home, resolv.conf, and devpts, uses private copies of
#   /etc/hosts and /etc/resolv.conf, but keeps mount tmp, proc, sys, and dev.
#   APPTAINER_BINDPATH and APPTAINER_MOUNT from the caller's environment are
#   still passed to %post.
#   This DEF therefore mounts private tmpfs over /tmp and /var/tmp first
#   (in %post, and in %test when it runs as root, as it does during builds),
#   fixes PATH, and sets HOME, TMPDIR, and XDG directories to the workspace
#   before any install step. It does not write /etc/hosts, /etc/localtime,
#   /dev, or /sys. The mount table is printed to the build log.
#   Production Apptainer version: 1.4.5 (supplied by the user). A local test
#   build (2026-09-30, GitHub Codespace, Apptainer 1.4.5 with the same
#   apptainer.conf, root build) succeeded, including %test. While building,
#   inotify and before/after listings showed no build-caused change in the
#   host /tmp or /var/tmp. Not performed: a build on the production build
#   machine or a --fakeroot build.
#   Build from a shell without APPTAINER_* or SINGULARITY_* bind variables.
#   %test checks R 4.6.1, Bioconductor 3.23, package loading, the exports
#   used by the scripts, a file-less PDF device, and conda/mamba on PATH.
#   These checks do not audit the entire filesystem or historical installation
#   activity.
#   The R version and Bioconductor release are pinned. Bioconductor patch
#   versions within 3.23, CRAN package versions, the Ubuntu tag, and APT
#   packages may change between builds. Installed R and Ubuntu package
#   versions are therefore recorded in the image. Full reproducibility needs
#   a CRAN snapshot/lock policy, which is not applied here.
#   Unresolved: the approved ubuntu:24.04 digest is not pinned yet; the CRAN
#   APT repository and Bioconductor are not yet registered approved recipes.
#
# [CHANGELOG]
#   2026-09-30 / 1.0: Created for ATAC_QC.1.0.R and ATAC_QC_plot.1.0.R
#   without Conda, using the fixed build workspace /__closha_build/work.
#   2026-09-30 / 1.0: Recorded the reported Apptainer admin bind settings
#   (home, /etc/localtime, /etc/hosts, user bind control) and moved the HOME,
#   TMPDIR, and XDG redirection to the start of %post, fixed PATH in %post,
#   and mounted private tmpfs over /tmp and /var/tmp so that no build step
#   can write to the host /tmp or /var/tmp. %test mounts the same private
#   tmpfs when run as root, because the build runs %test separately with
#   the host /tmp bound.
# =============================================================================

%labels
    Name bx_atac_qc
    Version 1.0
    RVersion 4.6.1
    BioconductorVersion 3.23
    BaseImage ubuntu:24.04
    InstallMethod "Ubuntu APT, CRAN Ubuntu APT R, BiocManager source packages"
    Description "R/Bioconductor environment for the CLOSHA ATAC_QC and ATAC_QC_plot scripts"

%environment
    export PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
    export LANG=C.UTF-8
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
    # Keep host-side user R libraries and profiles out of this runtime.
    unset R_LIBS
    export R_LIBS_USER=/usr/local/lib/R/site-library
    export R_PROFILE_USER=/dev/null
    export R_ENVIRON_USER=/dev/null

%post
    set -eu
    # Fixed container PATH; ignore any inherited PATH that may point into a
    # host-bound home directory.
    export PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8

    # Apptainer builds keep the admin "mount tmp = yes" setting, so %post sees
    # the host /tmp and /var/tmp. Cover both with private tmpfs mounts in this
    # container's mount namespace before any other command runs; the host
    # directories are then unreachable. If mounting fails, the build stops.
    mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-tmp /tmp
    mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-vartmp /var/tmp
    [ "$(stat -f -c %T /tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
    [ "$(stat -f -c %T /var/tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/var/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
    # Record the mount table in the build log for review.
    cat /proc/self/mountinfo

    fail() { echo "Build check failed: $*" >&2; exit 1; }

    # Fixed container-private workspace from the approved profile.
    # Plain mkdir (no -p) fails if a path already exists, including a symlink
    # or a bind mount point, so the build stops instead of reusing it.
    BUILD_ROOT=/__closha_build
    WORK=/__closha_build/work
    mkdir -m 0700 -- "$BUILD_ROOT"
    mkdir -m 0700 -- "$WORK"
    mkdir -p -- "$WORK/apt-cache/archives/partial" "$WORK/apt-lists/partial" \
        "$WORK/keys" "$WORK/tmp" "$WORK/home" "$WORK/r-cache" "$WORK/r-data" \
        "$WORK/r-config" "$WORK/biocmake-cache"

    # The admin config may bind the host home, and /tmp may be host-backed.
    # Redirect HOME, TMPDIR, and XDG directories into the workspace before any
    # other command runs, so no tool reads or writes host user files or /tmp.
    export HOME="$WORK/home"
    export TMPDIR="$WORK/tmp"
    export XDG_CACHE_HOME="$WORK/home/.cache"
    export XDG_CONFIG_HOME="$WORK/home/.config"
    export XDG_DATA_HOME="$WORK/home/.local/share"

    # APT package cache and index lists are redirected into the workspace.
    apt_ws() {
        apt-get -o Dir::Cache="$WORK/apt-cache" -o Dir::State::lists="$WORK/apt-lists" "$@"
    }

    # Use the official Ubuntu base; do not install Conda/Miniconda/Mamba.
    apt_ws update
    apt_ws install -y --no-install-recommends ca-certificates curl

    # CRAN Ubuntu repository key (fingerprint E298A3A825C0D65DFD57CBB651716619E084DAB9).
    # SHA256 was calculated from the key file published by CRAN.
    curl --fail --location --retry 3 \
        --connect-timeout 30 --max-time 120 \
        --output "$WORK/keys/marutter_pubkey.asc" \
        https://cloud.r-project.org/bin/linux/ubuntu/marutter_pubkey.asc
    printf '%s  %s\n' \
        ffa734347fd95fd7393f575448ba5e52cf3137067db77224d4857863351e4e8f \
        "$WORK/keys/marutter_pubkey.asc" | sha256sum --check -
    install -d -m 0755 /etc/apt/keyrings
    install -m 0644 "$WORK/keys/marutter_pubkey.asc" /etc/apt/keyrings/cran-ubuntu-marutter.asc
    printf '%s\n' \
        'deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/cran-ubuntu-marutter.asc] https://cloud.r-project.org/bin/linux/ubuntu noble-cran40/' \
        > /etc/apt/sources.list.d/cran-r.list

    # R 4.6.1 from CRAN, plus system libraries required by the R package set.
    apt_ws update
    apt_ws install -y --no-install-recommends \
        bash coreutils findutils grep sed \
        r-base-core=4.6.1-6.2404.0 r-base-dev=4.6.1-6.2404.0 \
        build-essential gfortran make cmake pkgconf \
        libcurl4-openssl-dev libssl-dev libxml2-dev libpng-dev libicu-dev \
        libgsl-dev libuv1-dev zlib1g-dev libbz2-dev liblzma-dev \
        libdeflate-dev libzstd-dev

    R --version | head -n 1 | grep -F 'R version 4.6.1'

    # R user caches stay in the workspace (HOME and TMPDIR are set above).
    # biocmake must use the APT cmake (>= 3.24) and not download its own.
    export R_USER_CACHE_DIR="$WORK/r-cache"
    export R_USER_DATA_DIR="$WORK/r-data"
    export R_USER_CONFIG_DIR="$WORK/r-config"
    export BIOCMAKE_CMAKE_COMMAND=/usr/bin/cmake
    export BIOCMAKE_CMAKE_CACHE_DIRECTORY="$WORK/biocmake-cache"

    # Install Bioconductor 3.23 packages into the image site library.
    # install.packages() only warns on failure, so loading is checked after.
    Rscript --no-init-file -e '
        options(repos = c(CRAN = "https://cloud.r-project.org"), Ncpus = 4L, warn = 1)
        lib <- "/usr/local/lib/R/site-library"
        if (!identical(normalizePath(.libPaths()[1]), lib)) {
            stop("unexpected first library path: ", .libPaths()[1])
        }
        install.packages("BiocManager", lib = lib)
        BiocManager::install(version = "3.23", ask = FALSE, update = FALSE, lib = lib)
        pkgs <- c("ATACseqQC", "ChIPpeakAnno", "Rsamtools", "GenomicAlignments",
                  "GenomicRanges", "GenomeInfoDb", "IRanges")
        BiocManager::install(pkgs, ask = FALSE, update = FALSE, lib = lib)
        ok <- vapply(pkgs, requireNamespace, logical(1), quietly = TRUE)
        if (!all(ok)) {
            stop("R packages failed to install: ", paste(pkgs[!ok], collapse = ", "))
        }
        if (!startsWith(as.character(packageVersion("BiocVersion")), "3.23.")) {
            stop("unexpected Bioconductor version: ", packageVersion("BiocVersion"))
        }
    '

    # Retain installed-version information with the image.
    mkdir -p /usr/local/share/bx-atac-qc
    R --version | head -n 1 > /usr/local/share/bx-atac-qc/r-version.txt
    Rscript --no-init-file -e '
        ip <- installed.packages()[, c("Package", "Version", "LibPath")]
        write.table(ip, "/usr/local/share/bx-atac-qc/r-packages.tsv",
                    sep = "\t", quote = FALSE, row.names = FALSE)
    '
    dpkg-query -W -f='${Package}\t${Version}\n' \
        > /usr/local/share/bx-atac-qc/ubuntu-packages.tsv

    # Remove only the exact workspace created above; stop on any doubt.
    # Each check is a separate command so that set -e cannot skip a failure.
    cd /
    [ "$WORK" = /__closha_build/work ] || fail "unexpected workspace path"
    [ ! -L "$BUILD_ROOT" ] || fail "parent is a symlink"
    [ ! -L "$WORK" ] || fail "workspace is a symlink"
    [ -d "$WORK" ] || fail "workspace is missing"
    [ "$(realpath -e -- "$WORK")" = "$WORK" ] || fail "canonical path changed"
    [ "$(stat -c %d -- "$WORK")" = "$(stat -c %d -- /)" ] || fail "workspace is on another filesystem"
    rm -rf --one-file-system -- "$WORK"
    rmdir -- "$BUILD_ROOT"

%runscript
    exec /usr/bin/Rscript "$@"

%test
    set -eu
    export PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8

    # The build runs %test separately from %post, again with the host /tmp and
    # /var/tmp bound (mount tmp = yes), and R and Python create temporary
    # files there. When running as root (a root or fakeroot build), cover both
    # with private tmpfs mounts first; if mounting fails, the build stops.
    # Unprivileged runtime checks cannot mount and skip this step.
    if [ "$(id -u)" = 0 ]; then
        mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-tmp /tmp
        mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-vartmp /var/tmp
        [ "$(stat -f -c %T /tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
        [ "$(stat -f -c %T /var/tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/var/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
    fi

    for cmd in R Rscript; do
        command -v "$cmd" >/dev/null 2>&1
    done

    R --version | head -n 1 | grep -F 'R version 4.6.1'

    # Load packages and check every pkg::function used by the scripts.
    # pdf(NULL) exercises the PDF device without writing a file.
    Rscript --no-init-file -e '
        pkgs <- c("ATACseqQC", "ChIPpeakAnno", "Rsamtools", "GenomicAlignments",
                  "GenomicRanges", "GenomeInfoDb", "IRanges")
        for (p in pkgs) suppressPackageStartupMessages(library(p, character.only = TRUE))
        if (!startsWith(as.character(packageVersion("BiocVersion")), "3.23.")) {
            stop("unexpected Bioconductor version: ", packageVersion("BiocVersion"))
        }
        if (!startsWith(as.character(packageVersion("ATACseqQC")), "1.36.")) {
            stop("unexpected ATACseqQC version: ", packageVersion("ATACseqQC"))
        }
        used <- c(
            "ATACseqQC::bamQC", "ATACseqQC::enrichedFragments",
            "ATACseqQC::fragSizeDist", "ATACseqQC::readBamFile",
            "ATACseqQC::shiftGAlignmentsList", "ATACseqQC::splitGAlignmentsByCut",
            "ChIPpeakAnno::estLibSize", "ChIPpeakAnno::featureAlignedDistribution",
            "ChIPpeakAnno::featureAlignedHeatmap", "ChIPpeakAnno::reCenterPeaks",
            "GenomeInfoDb::keepSeqlevels", "GenomeInfoDb::seqnames",
            "GenomicRanges::GRanges", "GenomicRanges::mcols", "GenomicRanges::seqnames",
            "IRanges::IRanges",
            "Rsamtools::BamFile", "Rsamtools::FaFile", "Rsamtools::ScanBamParam",
            "Rsamtools::close.FaFile", "Rsamtools::idxstatsBam", "Rsamtools::indexBam",
            "Rsamtools::indexFa", "Rsamtools::open.FaFile", "Rsamtools::scanBam",
            "Rsamtools::scanFaIndex"
        )
        for (u in used) {
            x <- strsplit(u, "::", fixed = TRUE)[[1]]
            invisible(getExportedValue(x[1], x[2]))
        }
        pdf(NULL)
        plot(1)
        invisible(dev.off())
        cat("ATACseqQC", as.character(packageVersion("ATACseqQC")), "\n")
    '

    # The build workspace must not remain in the image.
    if [ -e /__closha_build ]; then
        echo 'Build workspace /__closha_build remains in the image' >&2
        exit 1
    fi

    for cmd in conda mamba micromamba; do
        if command -v "$cmd" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
            echo "Unexpected package manager in image: $cmd" >&2
            exit 1
        fi
    done

    echo 'R 4.6.1 / Bioconductor 3.23: runtime dependency checks passed.'

%help
    CLOSHA ATAC QC environment: Ubuntu 24.04 + R 4.6.1 + Bioconductor 3.23
    (ATACseqQC, ChIPpeakAnno, Rsamtools, GenomicAlignments, GenomicRanges,
    GenomeInfoDb, IRanges). R comes from the CRAN Ubuntu APT repository;
    R packages are built from source. No Conda/Miniconda/Mamba is used.

    Build as an unprivileged user on a designated, internet-connected build
    machine matching the compute-node architecture. Do not bind production paths:
        apptainer build --fakeroot bx_atac_qc.1.0.sif bx_atac_qc.1.0.def

    Store the SIF, Apptainer cache, and build temporary files in an approved host
    build workspace. APPTAINER_CACHEDIR and APPTAINER_TMPDIR select the cache and
    temporary directories. Container cleanup must never target host-backed binds.

    Check the image:
        apptainer exec --cleanenv bx_atac_qc.1.0.sif R --version
        apptainer test --cleanenv bx_atac_qc.1.0.sif

    ATAC_QC.1.0.R and ATAC_QC_plot.1.0.R are supplied externally through
    approved runtime binds. This DEF does not run them during image construction:
        apptainer exec bx_atac_qc.1.0.sif Rscript ATAC_QC.1.0.R key=value ...
        apptainer exec bx_atac_qc.1.0.sif Rscript ATAC_QC_plot.1.0.R key=value ...

    ATAC_QC.1.0.R creates missing BAI files beside input BAM files and a missing
    .fai beside genome_fasta, so those locations must be writable unless the
    indexes already exist. ATAC_QC_plot.1.0.R reads BAM/RDS paths recorded in
    the ATAC_QC manifest, so the same paths must be bound at runtime.
    Both scripts remove previous output except logs/, so output_dir must be
    separate from the inputs and their parents. That existing deletion behavior
    must be reviewed separately before service use.
    Writable runtime binds can expose host data to the analysis scripts.
    Runtime analysis requires no network access.
